<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Sidmar buy of Ferrometalli Safem.</title>
<headline>EU clears Sidmar buy of Ferrometalli Safem.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had cleared the acquisition of Italian steel company Ferrometalli Safem SpA by Sidmar NV, a subsidiary of the Arbed group.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal Sidmar is buying 83.15 percent of the shares of Ferrometalli, currently owned by Falck.</p>
<p>The Commission noted that this wouild give Sidmar and Ferrometalli a share of less than six percent of the Italian market for flat steel products sold through stockholders and a total share of less than five percent of the overall Italian market for these products.</p>
<p>But it said that the companies would face competition from Riva and Usinor Sacilor as well as other Italian steel distributors.</p>
</text>
